// automations.memql -- the deploy pack (examples/deploypack), Epic 2.
//
// THE CORE PORT (E2.3 / #2096): the deploy lifecycle that
// component/deploycontrol/deploy.go + driver.go drive imperatively (pending ->
// in_progress -> observe the reconciliation -> succeeded | failed) is modeled
// here as event-driven DSL automations, keyed off the deployment status transition
// the CDC path emits (graph.node.updated.v1:cluster:deployment). Each transition
// fires the matching IntegrationProvider effect from E2.2 (#2095).
//
// MODEL A RECORD-BACK (E2.4 / #2097): after the pack commits the overlay and
// ArgoCD reconciles, the reconciled state (synced / healthy + per-node spec) is
// observed and recorded back into the deployment concept -- the GitOps-canonical
// loop. The committed overlay stays the source of truth; the data layer mirrors
// the observed state.
//
// SAFETY (live deploy path): the forward-deploy EFFECT these automations used
// to fire -- deployRunPromote -> Executor.RunPromote, the staging-to-prod
// digest pin -- went with the environment concept (epic memql#3943). A deploy
// is now the merge ArgoCD reconciles, so the terminal transition is decided by
// OBSERVING that reconciliation rather than by running anything.
// ADDITIVE: the Go orchestrator is NOT removed here (that is E2.5);
// these automations only load when the deploy pack is mounted (build tag
// `deploypack`), so they never fire in a default binary.
//
// SHAPE (#2400): decide -> act -> persist. The logic step decides AND fires the
// pack effect builtins, returning a flat outcome object; the gated mutation
// steps below persist the transition (logic performs no graph writes, per the
// behavioral-constructs ADR). Step calls use the kind-prefixed named-args form.

use deploypack.logic.{ driveDeploymentInProgress, recordReconciledState }
use deployment.mutations.{ updateDeploymentStatus }

@enabled
@trigger(event="graph.node.updated.v1:cluster:deployment")
@description("Event-driven port of deploy.go's transition: when a v1:cluster:deployment enters in_progress for the azure provider, observe ArgoCD's reconciled state and persist the terminal transition the logic decided -- succeeded (forward), rolled_back (rollback record), or failed. Epic 2 / #2096; decide->persist shape per #2400.")
automation driveDeploymentInProgress {
  step run {
    logic driveDeploymentInProgress(event: event)
  }
  step succeeded {
    if steps.run.result.outcome == "succeeded" {
      mutation updateDeploymentStatus(deploymentId: steps.run.result.deploymentId, status: "succeeded")
    }
  }
  step rolledBack {
    if steps.run.result.outcome == "rolled_back" {
      mutation updateDeploymentStatus(deploymentId: steps.run.result.deploymentId, status: "rolled_back")
    }
  }
  step failed {
    if steps.run.result.outcome == "failed" {
      mutation updateDeploymentStatus(deploymentId: steps.run.result.deploymentId, status: "failed")
    }
  }
}

// ---- automations/deploypack/recordReconciledState ----

@enabled
@trigger(event="graph.node.updated.v1:cluster:deployment")
@description("Model A record-back loop (#2097): when a v1:cluster:deployment reaches succeeded (the promote completed), observe the ArgoCD-reconciled state; the logic appends the per-node readiness via deployRecordBack on a clean reconciliation, and this automation persists the corrective failed transition when ArgoCD reports NOT synced/healthy (self-terminating -- the correction moves status off succeeded). Epic 2 / #2097; decide->persist shape per #2400.")
automation recordReconciledState {
  step run {
    logic recordReconciledState(event: event)
  }
  step correct {
    if steps.run.result.verdict == "correct" {
      mutation updateDeploymentStatus(deploymentId: steps.run.result.deploymentId, status: "failed")
    }
  }
}
